data={
'm8c09':('chem-m8-c09','How can mass and fragments constrain a structure?',
'''1. **blocker, scenes 12, 16 and notes.** The aid "rightmost is the molecule" sends a beginner to 66 in the very next attempt, where that answer is crossed out. Repair the aid and every repeated card to "Find the molecular-ion cluster. Tallest is the base." In feedback say "64 is M; 66 is its M+2 partner." Keep the chlorine scene. This replacement is length-neutral.
2. **should fix, scene 4.** "not from a heavier molecule" hides the actual cause of the isotope peak: the isotopologue is heavier. Replace with "It has the same structure, but a heavier carbon isotope." Use the same repair in scene 10 for chlorine. Cut the existing repeated clause about the electron's tiny mass to pay for any growth.
3. **should fix, scene 9.** The drawn butanone spectrum must use measured heights. The fragment at 57 is 8% in the retrieved NIST record, rather than 7%. Keep the diagram of the possible cleavage, but do not make its weak peak look like a major discriminator. The useful conclusion is that fragments support candidates, rather than prove them.''',
'''1. **blocker, scene 12 and notes.** "Rightmost is the molecule" contradicts the isotope cluster taught here. M+1 and M+2 are molecular ions too; the monoisotopic M is not the highest m/z. Repair as in learning finding 1.
2. **should fix, Numbers to verify.** Replace every height with `assets/brief120-mass-spectra.json`, backed by six saved NIST JCAMP records in `assets/brief120-nist/`. Butanone NIST 50206 has 43=100, 72=25, 29=17 and 57=8. Pentan-3-one NIST 227750 has 57=100, 29=59.40, 86=21.19, 27=12.39. Chloromethane NIST 18894 has 50=100, 15=72.38, 52=31.03, 49=11.41. Chloroethane NIST 19016 has 64=100, 28=83.01, 29=72.17, 27=60.46, 66=32.03, 49=26.62, 26=20.52. The site's 49 base-peak claim is false for this reference record. Butanal 43 and 72 both exceed 10%; that narrated comparison survives. Pentan-2-one 43 is the base peak; the attempt survives. Full weak-peak tables are in the JSON.
3. **should fix, scenes 4 and 10.** An isotope-containing molecule is heavier. Say "same structure, heavier isotope", rather than denying the higher mass.
4. **should fix, scene 2.** Electron impact does not knock an electron off every molecule. Replace "each molecule" with "some molecules" in both clauses. The neutral fraction is not steered or detected by this instrument.''',
'Primary measured source: [NIST chloroethane JCAMP](https://webbook.nist.gov/cgi/cbook.cgi?JCAMP=C75003&Index=0&Type=Mass). Other five exact URLs and NIST spectrum numbers are in the data JSON. Molecular formulas and nominal sums checked: 72, 86, 50/52, 64/66; gaps 29, 15 and 35. SDBS accession cross-check still pending.'),
'm8c10':('chem-m8-c10','How can IR distinguish the remaining functional-group candidates?',
'''1. **should fix, scene 12 and notes.** "No dip between sixteen eighty and seventeen fifty rules out every carbonyl compound" generalises the data-sheet window to every compound. Some carbonyl classes absorb outside it. Replace with "For these candidates, no carbonyl dip rules out the aldehyde or acid." Keep the named candidate structures visible. This is shorter and leaves both attempts answerable.
2. **should fix, scene 10.** "Amines have N H bonds" teaches an incorrect family rule. Tertiary amines have no N-H bond. Replace with "Primary and secondary amines have N H bonds"; replace "two small points" with "two N H bands" for the primary amine example. Pay for the extra words by shortening "side by side".
3. **should fix, scenes 6 to 11.** Eleven named traces need repeated structure recognition before each new band can be read. Keep the useful ethanol/acid comparison and the solved bottle. In each other scene retain only the current structure and trace, and dim all earlier range cards. Do not add more narration. Actual reading load and the three-bright-item rule remain untested until a build exists.''',
'''1. **should fix, scene 10.** Tertiary amines have no N-H bond. Replace "Amines" with "Primary and secondary amines". The two stretching bands are characteristic of the primary amine here, not all amines.
2. **should fix, scene 12 and notes.** The universal carbonyl exclusion is false outside the candidate set. Restrict the claim as in learning finding 1.
3. **blocker, spectrum data package.** The required eleven measured liquid-phase traces and per-band centre/depth/width comparison have not yet been completed. The memory-based depths cannot be passed as measurements. NIST ethanol Index 3, Coblentz 10139, was retrieved and explicitly identifies a 10% solution in CCl4/CS2, not a neat liquid film. It cannot silently validate the proposed hydrogen-bonded film O-H band. Ethanol SDBS 1300 identifies liquid-film record SDBS-IR2011-88120TK, but its curve has not been digitised. Deliver `assets/m8c10-ir-bands.json` only after checking actual phase and path length; do not fabricate %T values or treat ATR and transmission depths as interchangeable.
4. **should fix, visual in scene 5.** The current data-sheet table and recent exam axis conventions remain to be checked against the actual official exam PDF. The local syllabus is not the data sheet.''',
'[AIST ethanol record](https://sdbs.db.aist.go.jp/CompoundLanding.aspx?sdbsno=1300), accessed 30 October 2026. [NIST ethanol solution record](https://webbook.nist.gov/cgi/cbook.cgi?JCAMP=C64175&Index=3&Type=IR). No precise liquid-film band measurements are claimed.'),
'm8c11a':('chem-m8-c11a','How can carbon environments and shifts distinguish isomers?',
'''1. **should fix, scene 11 and notes.** "Further left means closer to an electronegative atom" becomes a general decision rule even though the displayed table includes alkene and aromatic carbons. Replace with "Further left means more deshielded. Check the data-sheet group." This is length-neutral and preserves the earlier oxygen cause chain.
2. **should fix, scene 6 and attempt 1.** A rotating cartoon by itself does not establish chemical equivalence. Keep every atom and bond in view and show that the entire labelled molecular structure matches after the swap, including the OH position. The student must be able to explain why swapping the ends of propan-1-ol fails. No added narration is needed; use the existing contrast.
3. **optional, scene 8.** The rare carbon-13 pair and decoupling are two different reasons for simplified spectra. Visually separate their insets so a student does not infer that low abundance causes proton decoupling.''',
'''1. **should fix, scene 11.** Electronegativity alone does not explain all chemical shifts; the displayed alkene/aromatic rows already refute the absolute memory line. Use the replacement in learning finding 1.
2. **should fix, scene 2.** In an ordinary field, the spin population difference is tiny. "Most pointing with the field, some against" should be drawn nearly balanced, with only a small excess in the lower state. Do not use a conspicuous majority as a population model.
3. **blocker, numerical spectrum verification.** Actual SDBS carbon spectra and assignments have not all been inspected. Proposed one-decimal shifts must remain provisional until solvent and accession are recorded for each compound. Environment counts were independently reconstructed: ethanol 2; propan-1-ol 3; propan-2-ol 2; butanone 4; pentan-3-one 3; ethyl ethanoate 4; tert-butanol 2; butan-1-ol 4; butan-2-ol 4; isobutanol 3; methyl ethanoate 3; propanoic acid 3. Both candidate deductions work by count and the O-bound-carbon contrast. The official data-sheet ranges still require direct exam-table comparison.''',
'[AIST ethanol SDBS 1300](https://sdbs.db.aist.go.jp/CompoundLanding.aspx?sdbsno=1300) lists several carbon spectra, including SDBS-NMR-CDS-00-245. The [original solvent-impurity study table hosted by UCSB](https://nmr.chem.ucsb.edu/docs/NMR_Impurities.pdf) supports ethanol values near 58 and 18 but also demonstrates solvent dependence. Other exact shifts remain unverified.'),
'm8c11b':('chem-m8-c11b','How do proton signals, areas and splitting reveal connections?',
'''1. **should fix, scene 5 and memory aid.** The narration first says areas give ratios, but the aid later says "areas count hydrogens". Replace the aid with "Signals count environments, areas compare hydrogens, lines count equivalent neighbours plus one." Keep the formula-to-ratio scaling from feedback 2 visible as the worked application. This adds useful characters and preserves the 5,500-character floor.
2. **should fix, scene 7 and notes.** The n+1 rule needs its simple-case condition before students generalise it to every neighbouring hydrogen. Replace the rule with "For these simple spectra, n equivalent neighbouring hydrogens give n plus one lines." Keep OH exchange shown as the stated exception. Do not remove other narration: the source is only 53 characters above the floor.
3. **optional, scene 9.** The separate quartet trap is useful because it distinguishes the measured set from its neighbours. Retain it; do not cut this to re-teach shielding from c11a.''',
'''1. **should fix, memory aid and key note 4.** Integration is a relative ratio before the molecular formula establishes actual counts. "Areas count hydrogens" should say "areas compare hydrogens". A triplet/quartet pair alone is not universal proof of an isolated ethyl group; use it as a candidate pattern checked against all clues.
2. **blocker, measured NMR package.** The exact proton shifts and line patterns for ethanol, bromoethane, ethyl ethanoate, methyl propanoate and pentan-3-one still require inspected SDBS records with solvent, field and accession. The OH shift cannot be fixed universally at 2.6 ppm. Do not claim these memory values have been verified.
3. **should fix, feedback 2.** "Only two signals means the molecule is symmetrical" is too broad as a universal rule because accidental overlap is possible. In this candidate comparison say "Of these candidates, two signals select the symmetrical pentan-3-one." This is longer and retains the floor.
The simple splitting predictions were reconstructed: ethanol CH3 triplet/CH2 quartet/exchanging OH singlet; bromoethane 3H triplet/2H quartet; ethyl ethanoate 3H singlet/2H quartet/3H triplet; methyl propanoate OCH3 singlet/CH2 quartet/end CH3 triplet; pentan-3-one 6H triplet/4H quartet, reduced ratio 3:2. These are structural checks, not measured-spectrum verification.''',
'[AIST ethanol record](https://sdbs.db.aist.go.jp/CompoundLanding.aspx?sdbsno=1300) identifies SDBS-NMR-HSP-01-876 and other proton records. Exact curves and the other compounds are pending.'),
'm8b12':('bio-m8-b12','How does each diabetes management action address the mechanism or its harm?',
'''1. **blocker, scene 2.** "muscle, liver and fat cells ... fewer glucose transporters move" gives the liver the muscle/fat mechanism. Replace with "In muscle and fat cells, insulin still binds, but fewer glucose transporters reach the membrane. The liver also releases too much glucose." Keep separate tissue arrows; do not animate GLUT4 recruitment in liver cells. Cut the repeated "Beta cells cover" sentence if needed for length.
2. **blocker, scene 9.** The 46/36/13 connected curve presents different denominators as one follow-up series. Replace the last point with a separate card "5-year extension: 11 of 85, 13%". Say "Among 85 people followed with continued support, 11 were in remission at five years." Keep the one- and two-year trial bars separate. Cut the generic trial-versus-everyday comparison bars to pay for this explanation.
3. **should fix, scene 8.** The dots randomly split as individuals, but randomisation was by GP practice. Group dots into practice clusters, randomise those clusters and say "GP practices were randomly assigned". This is length-neutral.
4. **should fix, scene 6.** Replace "red cells last about three months" with "red cells last about four months". Keep the distinct two-to-three-month weighted glucose window.''',
'''1. **blocker, scene 2.** GLUT4 recruitment belongs to muscle and fat, not the liver. The liver predominantly uses GLUT2. Repair the causal sentence and visual as in the learning review. [Original insulin cell-biology review](https://doi.org/10.1083/jcb.201802095).
2. **blocker, scene 9.** DiRECT's 13% is 11/85 extension participants with data, not the original intervention group. The original trial's 46% and 36% cannot be connected to it as one consistent cohort. The five-year paper also reports 12/118 (10%) among original intervention participants with available data. Use the explicit extension denominator and separate presentation. [Primary five-year paper](https://doi.org/10.1016/S2213-8587(23)00385-6). One/two-year figures are supported by the [trial team's site](https://www.directclinicaltrial.org.uk/).
3. **should fix, scene 6.** Red-cell lifespan is about 120 days; HbA1c estimates recent 8 to 12 weeks with greater weighting to recent glucose. [NIH explanation](https://www.niddk.nih.gov/health-information/professionals/diabetes-discoveries-practice/interpreting-a1c-principles-of-a1c-assay).
4. **should fix, scene 8.** Randomisation was by practice, not individuals. Label the allocation accurately. Remission should mean glucose below the diabetes diagnostic threshold without glucose-lowering medication, not necessarily normal glucose. Replace the gloss with "below the diabetes threshold without glucose-lowering medicines".
5. **should fix, scene 10.** "they're injected" is false for the whole GLP-1 drug class: oral semaglutide exists. Say "many are injected". Cardiovascular benefit is not identical for every member of the class. Attribute it to particular drugs in high-risk trial populations rather than to all GLP-1 medicines.
Metformin's liver action, improved insulin response and low hypoglycaemia risk are supported by [NIDDK](https://www.niddk.nih.gov/health-information/diabetes/overview/insulin-medicines-treatments). The fictional attempt arithmetic is correct: 1.4 minus 0.3 = 1.1 percentage points; 1/8=12.5%.''',
'See primary sources linked in findings. Full drug-label checks and all author-logged site claims still require completion; this is not a whole-lesson science pass.'),
'm8b13':('bio-m8-b13','How can a prevention campaign change exposure, and what evidence supports its effect?',
'''1. **should fix, scene 8.** "no control group, because you can't keep half the country out of a campaign" teaches that comparison designs are impossible. Replace with "This national trend has no randomised control group. Other exposures and policies changed too." A staggered rollout or comparison region is possible. The repair is shorter.
2. **should fix, feedback 10d.** Risk checks can initially increase diagnosed diabetes, so "new diagnoses" without a time window or denominator can make effective detection look like prevention failure. Replace with "Measure activity first, then the rate of new diabetes over several years, using the same testing in comparison groups." Cut "reported separately for the groups most at risk" from this sentence only, while keeping that demand on the question card and equity board.
3. **optional, scenes 2 and 5.** Keep the separate prevention levels and evidence levels visually distinct. Primary/secondary/tertiary are actions; process/impact/outcome are measures. One shared three-box motif without headings could make students pair them incorrectly.''',
'''1. **should fix, scene 8.** A lack of a randomised national control group does not mean controls cannot be used for campaigns. Give the study's actual limitation, rather than an impossibility claim.
2. **should fix, scene 7.** Date the under-40 outcome statement and identify invasive melanoma. The primary Queensland study covers 1995 to 2014 and finds declining age-specific invasive melanoma incidence below 40, particularly later birth cohorts. It does not establish the precise national onset date from that window. [Primary registry study](https://doi.org/10.1002/ijc.31141). The national AIHW commentary describes a late-1990s decrease; use that date for the national statement. [AIHW](https://www.aihw.gov.au/reports/cancer/cancer-data-in-australia/contents/cancer-data-commentaries/melanoma-of-the-skin-in-australia).
SunSmart's 1988 start and the 1987 to 2017 Melbourne repeated surveys are supported by the [primary PLOS study](https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pmed.1002932). The TV-advertising association is supported by the [2008 original study](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/18201638/). These are observational associations, consistent with the lesson's package-level conclusion. Do not relabel them as randomised causal estimates.
3. **should fix, attempt 2 feedback.** Screening changes ascertainment of diabetes as well as health. State comparable testing and adequate follow-up before treating new diagnoses as an outcome measure.''',
'Primary registry and survey publications are linked above. Specific 1981 campaign history, solarium jurisdiction dates and every author-logged site passage still need their individual primary checks.'),
'm8b14':('bio-m8-b14','Does a genetic technology find risk, select an embryo or change genetic material?',
'''1. **blocker, scene 8.** "The change would reach every cell ... so it would pass down the generations" turns a possible heritable edit into guaranteed uniform inheritance. Replace with "An edit to an egg, sperm or early embryo can enter the child's germline and be inherited." Keep the inheritance pathway visible. This is shorter and avoids needing an extra mosaicism lesson.
2. **should fix, scene 4.** "What's prevented is the phenotype" suggests PKU has no phenotype after treatment. Replace with "The diet prevents the harmful effects of high phenylalanine. It does not remove the altered alleles." The untreated/treated phenylalanine contrast should remain visible.
3. **should fix, scene 8.** "the only approach that would correct the allele itself" contradicts somatic gene editing just introduced. Replace with "The difference is inheritance: a germline edit could be passed to children." This is length-neutral.
4. **should fix, scene 6.** The PGT procedure is the important worked case. Keep the source embryo and extracted outer cells visible through biopsy, testing and selection. Use the freed time from finding 1 to pause once at "no embryo's DNA is changed". No need to add prenatal testing: it is not explicitly required by this dotpoint.''',
'''1. **blocker, scene 8.** Germline editing can cause mosaicism; an early-embryo edit does not necessarily reach every cell or pass to every descendant. Repair the guarantee as in learning finding 1. [NHGRI](https://www.genome.gov/about-genomics/policy-issues/Genome-Editing/ethical-concerns).
2. **should fix, scene 8.** Somatic editing can also correct an allele. The distinction is heritability, not whether the allele can be corrected. The Casgevy example specifically modifies BCL11A regulation to increase fetal haemoglobin rather than repairing the sickle HBB allele. [FDA label](https://www.fda.gov/media/174615/download?attachment=).
3. **should fix, new AAV plate brief.** AAV packages linear single-stranded DNA, not a closed DNA loop. Change only the internal DNA shape to a short open strand. Keep the non-enveloped icosahedral capsid. The vector's DNA largely persists episomally after delivery, which does not make its packaged genome a loop. [FDA Zolgensma label](https://www.fda.gov/media/126109/download), [TGA](https://www.tga.gov.au/resources/auspmd/zolgensma).
4. **should fix, scene 3.** PKU is not always complete absence of working enzyme. Say "too little working enzyme". A low-phenylalanine diet reduces intake; it does not remove every molecule of an essential amino acid. In scene 4 replace "removes the substance" with "limits the substance".
Medicare CF/SMA/fragile-X screening since 1 November 2023 is confirmed: [MBS items 73451/73452](https://www9.health.gov.au/mbs/fullDisplay.cfm?q=PN.7.16&qt=noteID&type=note). Mackenzie's Mission is much broader than three conditions: its primary design paper states 1,281 genes, and the study outcome page reports 9,107 couples. [Primary study](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9698511/), [study team](https://www.mackenziesmission.org.au/outcomes/).
The carrier cross is correct: Aa x Aa gives affected aa probability 1/4 per pregnancy. The current NSW panel count, PGT procedural source, Huntington treatment status and exact current Australian Act text still need direct checks.''',
'Primary sources are linked above. No claim of complete medicine, legal or panel verification is made. No prenatal-testing coverage blocker was found in the official dotpoint.'),
'm8b15':('bio-m8-b15','Where is the hearing pathway damaged, and which device can bypass that part?',
'''1. **should fix, scene 2.** "malleus, incus, stapes, in alphabetical order" is a false mnemonic. Remove "in alphabetical order". Retain the true anatomical sequence, with each bone highlighted from the eardrum to the oval window. This saves time.
2. **should fix, scene 5 and scene 9.** "the whole path must work" contradicts the fact hearing aids assist ears with partial hair-cell damage. Replace with "enough of the sound pathway must still work". Keep the healthy/damaged hair-cell comparison visible so loudness versus complete bypass has a physical referent.
3. **should fix, scene 7.** The electrode count comparison must not imply 1 electrode substitutes for exactly 1 hair cell, or electrode count alone determines sound resolution. Keep the two rows labelled "electrical channels" and "sensory cells" and say "a small number of electrical channels replaces the cochlea's much richer coding". Use the time saved in finding 1; if necessary cut the commercial-history timeline tag from learner-facing content.
4. **optional, scene 9.** Preserve the device-matching board and the short respectful account of Deaf perspectives. These serve the evaluate demand; there is no reason to add a separate ethics scene.''',
'''1. **should fix, scene 2.** Malleus, incus, stapes is the anatomical sequence, not alphabetical order. Correct the mnemonic in narration and any notes. [NIH sound pathway](https://www.nidcd.nih.gov/health/how-do-we-hear).
2. **should fix, scene 5.** Hearing aids are not restricted to mild-to-moderate loss. Prescription devices can assist severe loss when sufficient residual function remains. Replace "It suits mild to moderate loss of either kind" with "It can help when enough usable hearing remains." [NIDCD hearing aids](https://www.nidcd.nih.gov/health/hearing-aids). The mild-to-moderate restriction is specific to OTC devices.
3. **should fix, scene 9.** "the whole path must work" overstates the necessary condition. A damaged pathway with residual function can still be aided. Use "enough ... still work".
The core hair-cell-to-nerve cause chain, cochlear-implant bypass and need for rehabilitation are supported by [NIDCD](https://www.nidcd.nih.gov/health/cochlear-implants). Clark's team, Melbourne and its first patient on 1 August 1978 are supported by the [University of Melbourne](https://mdhs.unimelb.edu.au/150/impact/cochlear) and [original 1978 surgical paper](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/732655/). The narration avoids a world-first claim correctly. The device-specific 12-to-22 electrode range, 3,500 inner hair cells, 1982 commercial date and bone-conduction candidacy still require their individual sources; do not mark these numbers passed from the general NIH page.''',
'NIH, the treating hospital/university history and the original surgical paper were checked. Device-specific and commercial-history details remain pending.')
}
for key,(source,question,learning,science,sources) in data.items():
 a=audit[source]
 common=f'Independent AI reviewer, 30 October 2026. Input: `../lessons/{source}.md`, Revision 1. Inspected written narration and shot plans, not a built lesson, stills or continuous voiced preview. Narration recounted from `> ` lines with bold markers removed: {a["characters"]:,} characters; {len(a["scenes"])} narrated headings; no U+2014. Per-scene counts: `../assets/brief120-source-audit.json`. Human listening and learner testing are pending. Motion and caption fit cannot pass from a design document.\n\nMain learner question: {question}\n'
 for kind,body in [('learning-review',learning),('claude-science-check',science)]:
  tail='\n\n## Sources and unfinished verification\n\n'+sources if kind=='claude-science-check' else '\n\n## Review limits\n\nThis is a source review. Planned countdowns keep the question visible and notes have a separate quiet hold; actual answer concealment, visual references, reading load and motion remain preview checks. Sister-lesson comparison has not been fully completed. Findings above must be resolved before any source pass.\n'
  text=f'# {key} {kind.replace("-"," ")}\n\n'+common+'\n## Findings\n\n'+body+tail+'\n\n## Resolution\n'
  (base/'checks'/f'{key}-{kind}.md').write_text(text,encoding='utf8')
print('Wrote 16 review files, explicitly incomplete where primary checks remain.')
